The University of Bath is undertaking preliminary market engagement to inform the development of a future procurement for the provision of air conditioning and refrigeration maintenance, repair, compliance, replacement and installation services across its estate.
The anticipated scope includes planned preventative maintenance (PPM), reactive maintenance, emergency call-out services, statutory inspections, F-Gas compliance management, condition surveys, asset management support, equipment replacement, and installation works associated with air conditioning and commercial refrigeration systems.
Through this engagement, the University wishes to better understand:
- Current contractual arrangements operating within the region;
- Supplier capacity and capability to deliver services across the required geographic area;
- Preferred service delivery models, including self-delivery, subcontracted and hybrid approaches;
- Commercial and pricing models, including fixed-price, schedule of rates, target cost and performance-based arrangements;
- Supplier approaches to compliance management, asset lifecycle planning, sustainability, and innovation;
- Opportunities to improve service quality, operational efficiency, and value for money.
The scope excludes:
- Specialist laboratory refrigeration and environmental control equipment;
- Retail refrigeration and display merchandising equipment;
- Catering and commercial kitchen refrigeration equipment.
This engagement is intended to gather market intelligence and supplier feedback to support the development of the University's procurement strategy. It does not constitute a call for competition, nor does it commit the University to commencing a procurement process.
For more information about this opportunity, please visit the eSourcing portal at: 
https://www.delta-esourcing.com/tenders/UK-UK-Bath:-Heat-exchange-units%2C-air-conditioning-and-refrigerating-equipment%2C-and-filtering-machinery./N2G7CTMA57
To respond to this opportunity, please click here: 
https://www.delta-esourcing.com/respond/N2G7CTMA57

NHS Blood and Transplant (NHSBT) is undertaking preliminary market engagement in relation to a potential procurement for an enterprise-wide Digital Archiving & Storage Solution and associated services.
NHSBT is seeking to understand the market's capability to provide a secure, scalable and governed approach to the long-term retention, management, preservation, discovery and retrieval of digital information across the organisation.
The anticipated scope may include:
provision of an enterprise Digital Archiving & Storage platform;
discovery, implementation, configuration and deployment;
migration and onboarding of structured and unstructured data from existing applications, storage locations and legacy repositories;
long-term digital preservation capabilities;
information governance, retention, legal hold and controlled disposal;
search, retrieval, export and audit capabilities;
integration with NHSBT's existing technology estate;
professional and advisory services covering archive strategy, information lifecycle management, records management and operating model development;
service management, support and maintenance;
training and knowledge transfer; and
exit, data portability and transition services.
NHSBT's current requirement anticipates the solution supporting business, corporate and operational functions across the organisation. The procurement is intended to reduce risks associated with unmanaged data growth, legacy storage approaches and inconsistent retention practices while supporting information governance, security, regulatory compliance and future digital transformation.

